@@ -438,7 +438,22 @@ All loaders are subclasses of :class:`BaseLoader`.  If you want to create your
 own loader, subclass :class:`BaseLoader` and override `get_source`.
 
 .. autoclass:: jinja2.BaseLoader
-    :members: get_source, load
+    :members: get_source, load, list_templates, add_filter,
+        clear_filters, filter_scope
+
+Supported builtin listings accept persistent ``add_filter`` exclusions.
+Strings use case-sensitive globs, regex patterns search, and callables
+exclude a name when truthy. ``clear_filters`` restores the unfiltered
+listing. Filtering never prevents direct template loading. Child listing
+filters apply before a prefix or choice loader applies its own filters.
+Loaders without enumeration support still raise ``TypeError``.
+
+``filter_scope(*patterns)`` adds exclusions temporarily. Nested scopes,
+failed entry, and body exceptions restore the entering configuration;
+changes inside a scope are temporary. This synchronous loader-local
+context does not isolate threads or asynchronous tasks. It can select a
+compilation subset without changing the compilation error policy.
+``Environment.list_templates`` retains its separate one-shot filtering.
 
 Here a list of the builtin loaders Jinja provides:
 
